{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c355","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbc-2826-7673-94d4-717956fa0d32"},"sequence":5,"recorded_at":1780531400000005,"record_type":"status","durability":"ephemeral","causation_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","payload_type":"turn.input.user","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"turn_input_user","command_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b"},"prompt":"# Agent Task Assignment\n\n## FIRST — Run Immediately\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'set_status(TASK-260830-14yo67, status=reviewing)'\n```\n\n## Operational Constraints (Headless Run)\n\n- Never background a long command and end your turn: a headless session ends with\n  the turn and the process dies with it, while the run is still recorded as\n  completed with no evidence attached.\n- A single shell call is time-bounded (~10 minutes). Split long checks into\n  bounded sequential calls (package subsets, `-run` masks) and state explicitly\n  what you reran yourself versus accepted from already-attached evidence.\n- Attach evidence before you end the lifecycle, not after: \"I will attach it when\n  the run finishes\" is unfulfillable by construction.\n\nRun `task-board spawn directives \"$TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID\"` at safe checkpoints,\nat most once per 1 minute, never in a loop.\nDirectives have no delivery timer.\nSave before cancel; pause/reroute safely.\nIf reading directives fails, report unknown; do not treat it as none.\n\n\n## Role Contract\n\n- **Role:** `reviewer` (`reviewer`) — Reviews implementation quality and project fit\n- Obey task scope, acceptance criteria, and checklist.\n- Report real exit codes; failing gates stay failing.\n- Use scoped board projections; skip `summary()`,\n  `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`. Request scoped schema only after an\n  unknown call.\n- Load only relevant and explicitly required skills.\n\n### Skills\n\n- `project-management`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/project-management/SKILL.md`\n- `architecture-diagrams`: `/Users/iv/.claude/skills/architecture-diagrams/SKILL.md`\n\n### Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] Production entry points implement the scoped deliverable: Capture typed checkpoint closure over provider identity, workspace manifests, task-board bundle, terminal evidence, and source head\n- [ ] Relevant positive, negative, compatibility, and recovery tests pass with logs attached\n- [ ] README/doctor/capability evidence and specification traceability are updated without unsupported claims\n- [ ] Code written per task description and AC\n- [ ] Relevant tests written for new or changed behavior and passing\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Every command, message, state, or refusal named in the AC is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test, or is declared a stated bound. Report coverage as a ratio — `n of m AC rows driven` — and name the production call site for each. Prose in place of the ratio is not evidence.\n- [ ] Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior covered by negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject, with the production call site named\n- [ ] Every gate ships at least one NARROWING mutant — the gate stays present and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and a named test must fail. A delete-only mutant proves only that the gate exists and is not accepted as evidence.\n- [ ] A gate that inspects source text is additionally attacked by a mutant that PRESERVES the searched-for token and changes behavior, and the mutant harness executes the behavioral suite, not only the static checker.\n- [ ] Lint clean\n- [ ] Relevant build/validation commands run after changes and build not broken\n- [ ] New outcome artifact attached on the board with a task-scoped name when the work produces notes, logs, screenshots, or other deliverables\n- [ ] Important findings, decisions, anomalies, or regressions recorded in logbook when relevant\n- [ ] Implementation matches AC\n- [ ] Solution fits project architecture\n- [ ] Tests green\n- [ ] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n- [ ] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-14yo67\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-14yo67: implement-workspace-checkpoint-records\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-2rqigd\n\n### Description\n\nCapture typed checkpoint closure over provider identity, workspace manifests, task-board bundle, terminal evidence, and source head. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nrelux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); §5.4, §10.5-10.6, §13.12-13.13. Work only inside the workspace-checkpoints-and-operation-journal story boundary.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Capture typed checkpoint closure over provider identity, workspace manifests, task-board bundle, terminal evidence, and source head. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-14yo67_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-14yo67/TASK-260830-14yo67_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4914`\n- Content digest: `sha256:da3317dfa068ca33a0f3c1b552b4e5a8281d78971d33d4a6514c628c6b4ed144`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-14yo67_reviewer-cr1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-14yo67/TASK-260830-14yo67_reviewer-cr1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `6356`\n- Content digest: `sha256:37079df36bb6f07ad37012942ad6e0fa2db0b98538b9cc1293b5acece87ed15b`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-14yo67_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-14yo67, name=TASK-260830-14yo67_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- You are licensed to attempt to DEFEAT any gate, refusal, validation, authorization, or attestation under review, and to reject a change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a guard is in force; a delete-only mutant proves existence, not coverage.\n- Review read-only and record exactly one evidence-backed verdict: accepted → `done`; changes requested → `to-dev` or `analysis`; genuine Stop-The-Line → `blocked`. Never leave the task in `reviewing`.\n- With a `Change Request Under Review` section, accept via `task-board m 'accept_cr(ID, revision=N, evidence=ID_review-verdict.md)'`. It writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically and routes the element to `integrating` — accepted work never stays in `reviewing` and never reaches `done` from here. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype; only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it, and the orchestrator routes that run but does not close the leaf. `accept_cr` takes no acknowledgement argument, and only the reviewer run that was handed the revision may call it.\n- Reviewer-archetype runs must not supply `commit_ack` and must not escalate the commit-or-acknowledge decision to the human; record acceptance evidence and leave every `done` transition to the producer side.\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-2rqigd.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-2rqigd/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2rqigd`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Change Request Under Review\n\n- Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-14yo67-1` revision `1` (state `ready`)\n- Element: `TASK-260830-14yo67`, integration scope: `STORY-260830-2rqigd`\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2rqigd`\n- Base OID: `62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e`\n- Candidate tree OID: `1bef15e8461a035825d72c67e7ab97555f3ee0be`\n- Repository delta: `present`\n- Patch resource: `TASK-260830-14yo67_change-request_rev1.patch` (sha256 `f49ac905b59fbc2fa014800efbb5a00ee76367e3e9d02498ff9398c6343a849d`)\n\n```bash\ngit -C . diff 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e 1bef15e8461a035825d72c67e7ab97555f3ee0be          # the exact reviewable delta\ngit -C . diff --stat 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e 1bef15e8461a035825d72c67e7ab97555f3ee0be   # its shape\n```\n\nChanged paths (10):\n\n- `LOGBOOK.md`\n- `internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md`\n- `internal/sessckpt/capture.go`\n- `internal/sessckpt/capture_test.go`\n- `internal/sessckpt/crash_test.go`\n- `internal/sessckpt/crash_unix_test.go`\n- `internal/sessckpt/doc.go`\n- `internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py`\n- `internal/sessckpt/refusal_test.go`\n- `internal/sessckpt/store.go`\n\n### Recording the verdict\n\nAcceptance is a named mutation, not a status change:\n\n```bash\ntask-board m 'accept_cr(TASK-260830-14yo67, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-14yo67_review-verdict-rev1.md)'\n```\n\n`accept_cr` writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically: the Change Request becomes `accepted`, this run is stamped as the reviewer, and TASK-260830-14yo67 routes the element to `integrating` — accepted but not landed, and never `done`. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype (`developer`/`implementer`), and only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it. The orchestrator routes that run; it does not close the leaf, and no orchestrator run may execute the integration itself. `done` is produced only by the integration transaction, never by you and never by an acknowledgement. Never supply `commit_ack` yourself.\n\nChanges requested and Stop-The-Line are unchanged: route to `to-dev`/`analysis` or evidence-backed `blocked`. Leaving the element in `reviewing` is still not a verdict and still gets this run cancelled and respawned.\n"}}
