ecord 1.0.0 member set and order, the closure members (provider identity, workspace manifests, task-board bundle, terminal evidence, source head), the digest rules and the event-head binding from SPEC.v0.6.0.md yourself and diff them against capture.go/store.go; recompute the spec example's digest independently of the test fixture and confirm it equals the pinned value; confirm sections 10.5-10.6 and 13.12-13.13 clauses are each mapped to a driven test or an explicit stated bound. (2) Consumer admission — captured bytes must be admitted by the landed sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord and sessquery.admitCheckpoint (owning lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence variant, event heads at or before the owning lease) driven from the tests, not re-implemented; plant your own records through Capture/Admit: heads strictly after the owning lease, a creator that is not the holder, a persistence variant that disagrees with the session kind, a task-board bundle with a moved digest, a terminal-evidence member with the right name and wrong type, an unknown extra member — record admitted/refused with the exact code and layer for each. (3) Durability and idempotency — the install order is content-addressed blob (O_EXCL + fsync + directory sync) first, operation receipt second; rerun the three hook tests and the real-SIGKILL test twice; then use the BeforeWrite/AfterBlob/AfterCommit hooks with your own fault injection to leave (a) a blob without a receipt, (b) a receipt without a blob, (c) a torn blob — after restart Get/Admit must refuse or ignore each, never admit a partial record; same operation + identical inputs replays without any write (assert the directory mtime/inode set is unchanged), same operation + moved inputs refuses ErrCheckpointConflict with no write, different operation + identical inputs behaves as the spec says (state which clause); byte-identical reads across processes. (4) Refusal census — enumerate every refusal arm of Capture/Admit/Get/install/checkBoundary/checkDigestMember/checkPersistenceVariant/checkSessionKind; each needs a named test reaching it through the production entry with the exact code; attack the taxonomy: swap two adjacent arms sharing a code, swallow one arm into its sibling with a one-token edit, delete the `default` refusal in checkPersistenceVariant — the suite must go RED for each; report n-of-m with call sites. (5) Mutation — rerun mutant_harness.py in an isolated copy (7 of 7 KILLED claimed), rerun each KILLED twice for determinism, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (head-binding compare `<=` to `<`, session-kind check skipped for one kind, digest compare by prefix, receipt written before blob) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) Traceability and docs — the ownership registry internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json still binds section:5.4 to canonicaljson.validateCheckpointRecord with the gap text \"checkpoint creation and restore behaviour is not implemented\"; the producer left it untouched because the projection digest is review-pinned. Precedent Stories (3drr2m, 3jqsx1, 3m2mw8, 2jylym) updated the registry and re-pinned reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 inside the implementing Story: grade the stale row as P2 if any candidate document (README, LOGBOOK, TRACEABILITY.md, doc.go) claims Section 5.4 creation is implemented while the registry says it is not, otherwise P3 with the explicit requirement that a later leaf of this Story carries the registry update and digest re-pin before story_final; README has no entry for the new internal/sessckpt package — decide whether the repository's package documentation contract (every internal package with its test commands, see the sessrepo/sessstate sections) makes that a P3 to fix in this Story; LOGBOOK entry truthful, no CLI/capability claim. (7) Hygiene — changed_paths are exactly the candidate paths (new internal/sessckpt package, LOGBOOK.md), no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree; go test ./internal/sessckpt ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/sessquery -count=1 and -race green; go vet clean.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-14yo67/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-14yo67_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-14yo67_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-14yo67, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-14yo67_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
