{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c581","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbc-2826-7673-94d4-717956fa0d32"},"sequence":283,"recorded_at":1780531400000561,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adbc-baca-7071-977b-5a4da4c2560d"},"task_id":"01a0adbc-baca-7071-977b-5a4da4c2560d","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adbc-baca-7071-977b-5a4da4c2560d","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-14yo67 — implement-workspace-checkpoint-records: results\n2|\n3|Status: **ready for review** (developer → reviewer handoff).\n4|Worktree: `.temp/STORY-260830-2rqigd/worktree`, candidate left\n5|UNCOMMITTED. No CLI surface added; no commit on the Story branch.\n6|\n7|Authority: `relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0`\n8|(commit `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`);\n9|Sections 5.4, 10.5-10.6, 13.12-13.13 (headings retained from the\n10|v0.5.0 scope citations).\n11|\n12|## What was built\n13|\n14|New package `internal/sessckpt` (production):\n15|\n16|- `Store.Capture(chain, inputs)` — builds the typed checkpoint\n17|  closure (provider identity, workspace manifest, task-board\n18|  bundle, terminal evidence, source head) into a Checkpoint Record\n19|  1.0.0, attests it through `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`,\n20|  and installs it durably: content-addressed blob no-replace\n21|  (`O_EXCL` + fsync + directory sync) first, operation receipt\n22|  second. Same operation + identical inputs replays the recorded\n23|  checkpoint without writing; same operation + moved inputs\n24|  refuses `ErrCheckpointConflict` (`idempotency_mismatch`) and\n25|  writes nothing.\n26|- `Store.Admit(chain, raw, operationID, sessionKind)` — externally\n27|  built records (e.g. received through sync) through the same\n28|  attestation, variant, head-binding, and durability path.\n29|- `Store.Get(checkpointID)` — byte-identical reads re-verified\n30|  through the canonical owner on every read.\n31|- Crash hooks `BeforeWrite` / `AfterBlob` / `AfterCommit` (nil in\n32|  production), modeled on the `sessrepo` / TASK-260830-3qrfjp\n33|  durable-write discipline.\n34|\n35|Refusal taxonomy: `ErrInvalidCheckpoint` wraps\n36|`canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity` (`errors.Is` proves\n37|`incompatible_schema` for CP-N1..CP-N4 on both layers); unknown\n38|session/head propagate the `sessrepo` owner errors\n39|(`ErrUnknownSession` / `ErrUnknownEvent`); moved-input retries\n40|refuse `ErrCheckpointConflict`. Creator-holder binding is decided\n41|by the landed `sessquery.admitCheckpoint` consumer, which the\n42|tests drive on captured bytes (epoch-1 and successor positives\n43|through `BuildPlan`/`Revalidate`, wrong-creator refusal with\n44|`selector_observation_unavailable`).\n45|\n46|## AC coverage: 8 of 8 rows driven through the production entries\n47|\n48|| # | AC row | Call site | Tests |\n49|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n50|| 1 | provider identity | `Capture` → `checkBoundary` + manifest leg | `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord`, `TestCaptureTaskBoardVariantInstalls`, `bad_provider_id`, `empty_provider_version` |\n51|| 2 | workspace manifests | `Capture` → `checkDigestMember` | positives, `bad_workspace_manifest`, `TestCaptureMovedInputsChangeIdentity` |\n52|| 3 | task-board bundle | `Capture`/`Admit` → `checkPersistenceVariant` | task-board positive, 5-arm variant table, `Admit(bad kind)` |\n53|| 4 | terminal evidence | `Capture` → `checkBoundary` | 5-arm quiescence table incl. CP-N1, `bad_evidence` |\n54|| 5 | source head | `Capture`/`Admit` → head binding vs `sessrepo` chain | 2 consumer positives, unknown/later-lease/malformed-head tests |\n55|| 6 | exact fixtures + negatives | `Capture`, `Admit`, `Get`, `AttestCheckpointRecord` | spec example attests (digest pinned), CP-N1..CP-N4, malformed-frame/torn tests |\n56|| 7 | crash/idempotency | `Store.install` + hooks | 3 hook tests, real-SIGKILL test, conflict/disagreement/replay tests |\n57|| 8 | no unsupported capability | (no new surface) | stated bound: library only; README/doctor untouched, no CLI advertised |\n58|\n59|Full clause map: `internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md` (also attached\n60|as `TASK-260830-14yo67_conformance-matrix.md`).\n61|\n62|## Validation (all on the final source unless noted)\n63|\n64|- `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`: clean.\n65|- `go test ./... -count=1`: 27 packages ok (`full-test.log`).\n66|- `go test ./internal/sessckpt/ -race -count=1`: ok\n67|  (`sessckpt-race.log`); `-cover`: 81.8% (`sessckpt-cover.log`);\n68|  verbose package log (`sessckpt-verbose.log`).\n69|- Race for every other package: `race-rest.log` (all lighter\n70|  packages), `race-sessrepo.log`, `race-canonicaljson.log`,\n71|  `race-sessquery.log` — all ok.\n72|- Full cover: `cover-full.log`.\n73|- Narrowing mutants, shipped harness\n74|  `internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py`: **7 of 7 killed**,\n75|  1 harmless SURVIVED control, 0 NOT_APPLIED, 0 harness failures\n76|  (`mutants/` per-plant raw logs + `summary.json`).\n77|- `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck`: ok.\n78|- `cataloggen -check`: ok.\n79|- `task-board validate`: (see handoff transcript).\n80|- `gofmt -l`, `git diff --check`: clean.\n81|\n82|## Notable findings\n83|\n84|1. Own negative test caught a real bug: `Admit` first skipped the\n85|   session-kind check and admitted any kind. Fixed by routing\n86|   `Admit` through `checkSessionKind` plus a `default` refusal in\n87|   `checkPersistenceVariant` (`TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames/Admit(bad kind)`).\n88|2. Race flake in the new SIGKILL test: after `syscall.Kill(self,\n89|   SIGKILL)` the child fell through to `os.Exit(99)` before the\n90|   kernel acted (once, under `-race`). Fixed by blocking forever\n91|   after the kill; the parent carries a 60 s context timeout so a\n92|   failed kill is a timeout failure, never a false pass. Stable\n93|   across repeated race runs since.\n94|3. The `section:5.4` ownership-registry gap (\"creation ... not\n95|   implemented\") is now stale, but the registry projection digest\n96|   is review-pinned against self-minted claims, so the registry\n97|   text is deliberately untouched; the interim clause record is\n98|   `internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md` bound 5. Registry refresh\n99|   is left for review-gated maintenance.\n100|4. Storage-level faults (ENOSPC, torn volume) are a stated bound:\n101|   the install path follows the TASK-260830-3qrfjp model\n102|   (no-replace + fsync + torn-read refusal, all driven), with no\n103|   dedicated ENOSPC fault test in this package.\n104|\n105|## Files\n106|\n107|- `internal/sessckpt/doc.go`, `store.go`, `capture.go`\n108|- `internal/sessckpt/capture_test.go`, `refusal_test.go`,\n109|  `crash_test.go`, `crash_unix_test.go` (unix-only SIGKILL),\n110|  `TRACEABILITY.md`, `mutant_harness.py`\n111|- `LOGBOOK.md` (newest entry)\n112|- Evidence pack: `TASK-260830-14yo67_producer-evidence.tar.gz`\n113|  (test logs, mutant raw logs + summary, tracecheck/catalog logs)","final_result":true}}}
