ict stays with the consumer; tests drive the\n25|//     consumer on captured records instead of re-implementing it.\n26|//   - internal/scalar owns digest, UUID, and timestamp grammar.\n27|//   - internal/secconftest owns the crash-injection vocabulary the\n28|//     tests wire to the store hooks.\n29|//\n30|// Refusal taxonomy (SPEC Section 5.4: CP-N1..CP-N4 MUST be rejected\n31|// with incompatible_schema before publication):\n32|//\n33|//   - ErrInvalidCheckpoint wraps canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so\n34|//     errors.Is proves the incompatible_schema class for every\n35|//     unpublishable closure: malformed grammar, closed-shape\n36|//     violations, non-quiescent terminal evidence, missing or\n37|//     doubled persistence members, the wrong persistence variant\n38|//     for the declared session kind, and heads that postdate the\n39|//     owning lease.\n40|//   - Unknown sessions and unknown heads propagate the sessrepo\n41|//     chain-read errors (ErrUnknownSession, ErrUnknownEvent), so\n42|//     errors.Is preserves the owner's vocabulary.\n43|//   - ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the\n44|//     same operation retried with moved inputs, and a digest path\n45|//     holding disagreeing bytes.\n46|//\n47|// Durable-write model (TASK-260830-3qrfjp): content-addressed blobs\n48|// installed no-replace (O_EXCL) with fsync before close, operation\n49|// receipts installed no-replace after the blob they name, directory\n50|// fsync after install. A crash leaves either nothing, or complete\n51|// bytes that verify through the canonical owner; an interrupted\n52|// capture is resumed by retrying the same operation with\n53|// byte-identical inputs (safe_retry), never by inventing state.\n54|//\n55|// Stated bounds: the raw AdmitRecord path attests shape and the\n56|// variant/head gates it can decide, but chain binding needs the\n57|// caller's repository handle; a nil chain refuses closed rather\n58|// than skipping the gate. Capture does not consult lease records:\n59|// creator-holder binding is decided by the consumer at admission\n60|// (pinned by tests here). Capture performs no provider or\n61|// task-board I/O and offers no CLI surface.\n62|package sessckpt","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbc-2826-7673-94d4-717956fa0d32"},"sequence":325,"recorded_at":1780531400000645,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b"},"call_id":"call_01a0adbcc54b7793b339af5fd3859308","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/store.go`.\n1|package sessckpt\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|\t\"os\"\n7|\t\"path/filepath\"\n8|\t\"runtime\"\n9|\t\"sync\"\n10|\n11|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n12|)\n13|\n14|// ErrInvalidCheckpoint reports a checkpoint closure that must be\n15|// refused before publication. It always wraps\n16|// canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity, so errors.Is proves the SPEC\n17|// Section 5.4 incompatible_schema class for every unpublishable\n18|// closure, including the CP-N1..CP-N4 fixtures.\n19|var ErrInvalidCheckpoint = errors.New(\"invalid checkpoint closure\")\n20|\n21|// ErrCheckpointConflict reports the idempotency boundary: the same\n22|// capture operation retried with moved inputs\n23|// (idempotency_mismatch), or a digest path holding bytes that\n24|// disagree with the installing candidate (a torn store, never a\n25|// second version of an immutable record).\n26|var ErrCheckpointConflict = errors.New(\"checkpoint capture conflict\")\n27|\n28|// Store durably installs Checkpoint Records and their operation\n29|// receipts under one data root. Checkpoint blobs are\n30|// content-addressed and installed no-replace, so capture is\n31|// append-only by construction and there is no update or delete\n32|// entry to test.\n33|//\n34|// BeforeWrite fires after validation and before the first durable\n35|// byte; AfterBlob fires after the checkpoint blob is durable and\n36|// before the operation receipt; AfterCommit fires after the receipt\n37|// is durable. All three are nil in normal operation. Tests connect\n38|// them to a secconftest Injector firing the owner's own points: a\n39|// fault before any durable byte carries safe_retry, a fault past\n40|// any durable step carries recoverable_parked_state until the\n41|// identical retry replays the recorded result, and a fault past\n42|// the receipt carries safe_retry through the replayed receipt.\n43|type Store struct {\n44|\troot        string\n45|\tmutex       sync.Mutex\n46|\tBeforeWrite func() error\n47|\tAfterBlob   func() error\n48|\tAfterCommit func() error\n49|}\n50|\n51|// Open binds a checkpoint store to the checkpoints namespace beneath\n52|// dataRoot, creating it owner-only when absent. The root must be\n53|// absolute.\n54|func Open(dataRoot string) (*Store, error) {\n55|\tif !filepath.IsAbs(dataRoot) {\n56|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: data root %q is not absolute\", ErrInvalidCheckpoint, dataRoot)\n57|\t}\n58|\troot := filepath.Join(dataRoot, \"checkpoints\")\n59|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(root, 0o700); err != nil {\n60|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create checkpoints root %q: %w\", root, err)\n61|\t}\n62|\t// The operations namespace shares the root so one data-root\n63|\t// fsync discipline covers blobs and receipts together.\n64|\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Join(root, \"operations\"), 0o700); err != nil {\n65|\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"create checkpoint operations root: %w\", err)\n66|\t}\n67|\treturn &Store{root: root}, nil\n68|}\n69|\n70|// CheckpointRef names one durably installed Checkpoint Record: its\n71|// canonical digest and the operation receipt that installed it.\n72|type CheckpointRef struct {\n73|\tCheckpointID string\n74|\tOperationID  string\n75|}\n76|\n77|// checkpointFileName maps a validated checkpoint digest to its blob\n78|// file name. The digest passed scalar grammar before install;\n79|// invalid input maps to a sentinel name that can never collide\n80|// with a real blob.\n81|func checkpointFileName(checkpointID string) string {\n82|\tdigest, err := scalar.ParseDigest(checkpointID)\n83|\tif err != nil {\n84|\t\treturn \"invalid.json\"\n85|\t}\n86|\treturn digest.Hex() + \".json\"\n87|}\n88|\n89|// operationFileName maps a validated operation UUID to its receipt\n90|// file name. UUIDv7 grammar keeps the file name an exact,\n91|// case-stable rendering of the operation identity.\n92|func operationFileName(operationID string) string {\n93|\tid, err := scalar.ParseUUIDv7(operationID)\n94|\tif err != nil {\n95|\t\treturn \"invalid.json\"\n96|\t}\n97|\treturn id.String() + \".json\"\n98|}\n99|\n100|// installBlob installs one content-addressed blob idempotently\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5d7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbc-2826-7673-94d4-717956fa0d32"},"sequence":326,"recorded_at":1780531400000647,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b"},"call_id":"call_01a0adbcc62071fdbcf3c29b13892764","text":"Read text file `internal/sessckpt/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# `internal/sessckpt` traceability (TASK-260830-14yo67)\n2|\n3|Authority: `relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0`\n4|(`internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json`, embedded\n5|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`). The task scope cites the same\n6|section numbers of v0.5.0; the headings are retained in v0.6.0, so\n7|every row below names the pinned v0.6.0 heading. Historical v0.5.0\n8|behavior is preserved: the closed Checkpoint Record 1.0.0 member\n9|set is unchanged between the two revisions.\n10|\n11|Production entry points: `Store.Capture`, `Store.Admit`,\n12|`Store.Get` (`internal/sessckpt/capture.go`); durable install\n13|(`internal/sessckpt/store.go`). No CLI surface is offered; the\n14|`sessckpt` package is a library only.\n15|\n16|## AC coverage (8 of 8 rows driven through the production entries)\n17|\n18|| # | AC row | Production call site | Named tests |\n19|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n20|| 1 | Closure over provider identity | `Capture` → `checkBoundary` (provider_id/version) + `provider_manifest_id` leg | `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord`, `TestCaptureTaskBoardVariantInstalls`, `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_provider_id`, `/empty_provider_version` |\n21|| 2 | Closure over workspace manifests | `Capture` → `checkDigestMember(workspace_manifest_id)` | positives above, `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_workspace_manifest`, `TestCaptureMovedInputsChangeIdentity` |\n22|| 3 | Closure over task-board bundle | `Capture`/`Admit` → `checkPersistenceVariant` | `TestCaptureTaskBoardVariantInstalls`, `TestCaptureRefusesBadPersistenceVariant` (all five arms), `TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames/Admit(bad kind)` |\n23|| 4 | Closure over terminal evidence | `Capture` → `checkBoundary` (evidence enum + quiescence publication rule) | `TestCaptureRefusesNonQuiescentBoundary` (all five arms incl. CP-N1), `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_evidence` |\n24|| 5 | Closure over source head | `Capture`/`Admit` → `checkHeadBinding`/`checkRawHeadBinding` against `sessrepo.Repository.ListEvents` | `TestCaptureAdmitsThroughWinningLeaseConsumer`, `TestCaptureSuccessorAdmitsThroughConsumer`, `TestCaptureRefusesUnknownSessionAndHead`, `TestCaptureRefusesLaterLeaseHead`, `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedHeads` |\n25|| 6 | Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases | `Capture`, `Admit`, `Get` + `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord` | `TestSpecExampleAttestsThroughConsumerOwner`, `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord` (closed member set equals the normative example), CP-N1 (`cp_n1_background_idle_false`), CP-N2 (`cp_n2_direct_null_provider`), CP-N3 (`cp_n3_both_present`), CP-N4 (`TestAdmitRefusesUnknownSafeBoundaryMember` with benign re-identified control), `TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames`, `TestGetRefusesUnknownAndTorn` |\n26|| 7 | Crash/idempotency evidence for durable capture | `Store.install` (blob-first, receipt-second, no-replace) + `BeforeWrite`/`AfterBlob`/`AfterCommit` hooks | `TestCrashBeforeDurableWriteIsSafeRetry`, `TestCrashBetweenBlobAndReceiptResumes`, `TestCrashAfterReceiptReplaysRecordedResult`, `TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates` (real SIGKILL), `TestCaptureWithMovedInputsRefuses`, `TestCaptureRefusesDisagreeingDigestPath`, `TestCaptureReplayIsIdempotent`, `TestCaptureIdenticalClosuresShareIdentity` |\n27|| 8 | No unsupported capability advertised | no `cmd/` surface, no provider/task-board I/O in the package | Stated bound (see below); `gofmt`/`go vet`/`go build` clean, README/doctor untouched by this change |\n28|\n29|## Pinned-clause map\n30|\n31|### Section 5.4 Checkpoint Record\n32|\n33|| Clause | Owner / call site | Evidence |\n34|| --- | --- | --- |\n35|| Closed 16-member shape, `schema`/`schema_version` exact, `status` = `validated`, `subject_id` = `session_id` | `canonicaljson.validateCheckpointRecord` via `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord`; `buildCandidate` assembles exactly the closed set | member-set equality vs the normative example in `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord`; `TestSpecExampleAttestsThroughConsumerOwner` |\n36|| `checkpoint_id` canonical omit-self digest | `canonicaljson.CalculateObjectIdentity` + `AttestCheckpointRecord`, drift-checked in `identifyCandidate` | every positive test attests; `TestAdmitRefusesMalformedFrames/Admit(tampered)` |\n37|| Safe Boundary Evidence closed shape + publication rule (all idle true, counters zero) | `checkBoundary` first, owner backstop second | quiescence table; narrowing mutant `N-bg-idle` killed by `cp_n1_background_idle_false` |\n38|| Persistence variant: exactly one leg; direct↔provider, task_board↔bundle | `checkPersistenceVariant` (+ `checkSessionKind`) first, owner presence backstop second | variant table; mutants `N-both-present`, `N-swapped-direct` killed |\n39|| `event_heads` 1..64 sorted unique, resolving at or before the owning lease | `checkHeads` + `checkHeadBinding`/`checkRawHeadBinding` first, owner shape backstop second | heads table + unknown/later-lease tests; mutant `N-duplicate-heads`, `N-later-epoch-head` killed |\n40|| CP-N1..CP-N4 rejected with `incompatible_schema` before publication | `Capture`/`Admit` refuse `ErrInvalidCheckpoint` wrapping `canonicaljson.ErrInvalidIdentity` (`errors.Is` proves both layers) | rows above; mutant `N-evidence-enum` (token-preserving) killed by `bad_evidence` |\n41|| Normative example | attests through the same owner | `TestSpecExampleAttestsThroughConsumerOwner` (digest pinned) |\n42|| Owning lease tuple, creator-holder, variant, head closure at admission | `sessquery.admitCheckpoint` (landed consumer, not re-implemented) | epoch-1 + successor `BuildPlan`/`Revalidate` positives; wrong-creator refusal (`selector_observation_unavailable`) |\n43|| Force-takeover newest-validated-checkpoint selection | consumer behavior, out of capture scope | Stated bound: capture mints and installs; selection stays with the takeover owner |\n44|\n45|### Sections 10.5-10.6 Materialization Plan / Journal\n46|\n47|The checkpoint contributes its closure digests (`workspace_manifest_id`,\n48|`provider_manifest_id`/`task_board_bundle_id`, checkpoint digest,\n49|lease tuple) as plan source inputs; the plan/journal state machines\n50|are owned by sibling TASK-260830-3k3e6m. Capture binds the exact\n51|digest strings the plan rows consume and refuses to publish a\n52|closure no plan row could select (variant gate). No plan or journal\n53|bytes are written here: stated bound.\n54|\n55|### Sections 13.12-13.13 Failure matrix / crash-outcome gate\n56|\n57|| Applicable row | Capture behavior | Evidence |\n58|| --- | --- | --- |\n59|| Invalid digest/schema | refused before any durable byte (`ErrInvalidCheckpoint`) | all negative tests assert zero writes only where counted (`TestCrashBeforeDurableWriteIsSafeRetry` counts 0/0) |\n60|| Operator interrupt / crash before first byte | nothing mutated; identical retry safe (`safe_retry`) | injector `PointPrepareEnter` test |\n61|| Crash between blob and receipt | complete verifying blob, no receipt; identical retry completes (`safe_retry`) | hook test + real SIGKILL test (`TestCaptureCrashChildSelfTerminates`) |\n62|| Crash after receipt | recorded result replayed, no second identity (`safe_retry` via receipt) | hook test |\n63|| Retry with moved inputs | refuses `ErrCheckpointConflict` (`idempotency_mismatch`), writes nothing | `TestCaptureWithMovedInputsRefuses` + narrowing mutant `N-idempotency-session` killed |\n64|| Disk-full / rename-blocked / permission faults | install errors propagate; no-replace keeps existing blobs; torn bytes refuse attestation on read | Design property on the TASK-260830-3qrfjp durable-write model; torn-read path driven by `TestGetRefusesUnknownAndTorn` and `TestCaptureRefusesDisagreeingDigestPath`. No dedicated ENOSPC fault test in this package: stated bound (storage faults are owned with their fault model by `internal/localstore` + TASK-260830-3qrfjp) |\n65|| Two live owners for one session | out of capture scope (lease arbitration) | Stated bound |\n66|\n67|## Negative-evidence proofs\n68|\n69|Shipped harness: `internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py`. Run:\n70|\n71|    PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/sessckpt/mutant_harness.py --log-dir .temp/TASK-260830-14yo67/mutants\n72|\n73|Result on the delivered source: **7 of 7 narrowing mutants killed**,\n74|**1 of 1 harmless SURVIVED controls applied**, 0 NOT_APPLIED, 0\n75|compile/harness failures. Per-plant raw logs (command, return code,\n76|full output) live under the log dir with `summary.json`; the same\n77|logs ship in `TASK-260830-14yo67_producer-evidence.tar.gz`.\n78|\n79|| Plant | Weakening (admits exactly the named member) | Killer |\n80|| --- | --- | --- |\n81|| `N-bg-idle` | quiescence gate passes `background_idle=false` when no process is open | `TestCaptureRefusesNonQuiescentBoundary/cp_n1_background_idle_false` (own-gate message attribution; the owner backstop still refuses with different text) |\n82|| `N-both-present` | presence gate passes both-legs-present | `TestCaptureRefusesBadPersistenceVariant/cp_n3_both_present` (the kind gate then fires with different attribution) |\n83|| `N-swapped-direct` | direct arm passes bundle-only | `TestCaptureRefusesBadPersistenceVariant/swapped_direct_takes_bundle` (clean admission kill: capture succeeds) |\n84|| `N-duplicate-heads` | order gate passes duplicates (`<=` → `<`) | `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedHeads/duplicated` (own-gate `sorted unique` attribution; owner backstop text differs) |\n85|| `N-later-epoch-head` | epoch arm admits heads one epoch past the owner (`>` → `>+1`) | `TestCaptureRefusesLaterLeaseHead` (clean admission kill) |\n86|| `N-idempotency-session` | conflict gate passes moved inputs under the same session | `TestCaptureWithMovedInputsRefuses` (clean admission kill: retry succeeds) |\n87|| `N-evidence-enum` | closed enum admits exactly `provider_gossip`; every searched-for token preserved | `TestCaptureRefusesMalformedClosureMembers/bad_evidence` (own-gate `safe_boundary` attribution) |\n88|| `C-harmless-comment` | comment-only edit | `TestCaptureDirectInstallsAttestedRecord` still passes (SURVIVED) |\n89|\n90|## Stated bounds (not driven, declared)\n91|\n92|1. Raw `Admit` trusts the supplier for lease-tuple/creator truth the\n93|   way any sync-installed record does; the consumer re-decides\n94|   creator-holder at admission. Chain binding is still enforced\n95|   (nil chain refuses closed).\n96|2. Capture performs no provider, task-board, or terminal I/O: the\n97|   quiescence facts are caller-declared and the publication rule is\n98|   enforced on the declaration. Live observation belongs to the\n99|   provider/terminal owners.\n100|3. Manifest bytes are referenced by digest only; manifest resolution\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
