ther than blacklisted: `internal/config/sshargs.go` declares the\\n342:space is that injection one word-split away. `internal/config/endpoint.go`\\n383:    go test ./internal/config -count=1 -v\\n384:    go test ./internal/config -cover -count=1\\n385:    go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\\n395:[`internal/provider`](internal/provider) implements the Section 7.1 trusted\\n426:go test ./internal/provider -count=1\\n427:go test ./internal/provider -cover -count=1\\n434:against the digest-pinned document in `internal/specdoc`, quoting the exact\\n439:[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) implements the ax host side of\\n500:go test ./internal/provhost -count=1\\n501:go test ./internal/provhost -cover -count=1\\n518:arm, so a planted arm or a deleted branch reddens in either direction. This inventory is independent of the per-package refusal inventories in [`internal/provider`](internal/provider) above and [`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) below (see [Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate](#specification-to-code-ownership-gate)): each package derives its own refusal arms from its own source in its own test file, and the three share no inventory code or table.\\n525:[`internal/secprim`](internal/secprim) implements the shared safe\\n531:in [`internal/scalar`](internal/scalar) (the member gate delegates every\\n535:[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) (which delegates its\\n537:Error detail redaction stays in [`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror),\\n538:SSH argv admission stays in [`internal/config`](internal/config), and\\n540:[`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend). Trust for\\n596:anywhere under `internal/`, nested packages included — not the absence\\n618:go test ./internal/secprim -count=1\\n619:go test ./internal/secprim -cover -count=1\\n624:[`internal/secconftest`](internal/secconftest) is the test instrument\\n629:[`internal/scalar`](internal/scalar), every bound check in\\n630:[`internal/environ`