nt lease holder |\n2003|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp | Diagnostic only |\n2004|| <code>status</code> | enum | Literal <code>validated</code> |\n2005|| <code>extensions</code> | object | Reverse-DNS extension keys only |\n2006|\n2007|Safe Boundary Evidence is a closed object containing exactly\n2008|<code>provider_id:provider-id</code>,\n2009|<code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>,\n2010|<code>evidence:provider_api|provider_event|managed_pty|task_board_bridge|accepted_test</code>,\n2011|<code>input_blocked:boolean</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>,\n2012|<code>background_idle:boolean</code>, <code>open_processes:uint53</code>, and\n2013|<code>open_database_handles:uint53</code>. A published checkpoint requires all\n2014|three booleans true and both counters zero. Provider-specific scheduled or\n2015|child work is included in <code>background_idle</code> and\n2016|<code>open_processes</code>; an adapter that cannot prove it MUST NOT publish a\n2017|new checkpoint.\n2018|\n2019|The referenced Session Record selects the persistence variant. For\n2020|<code>kind = direct</code>, <code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be non-null\n2021|and <code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be null. A backend-resolved provider\n2022|with no portable bytes still uses a provider Transfer Manifest containing its\n2023|validated identity and zero file entries; null is not used to erase that\n2024|distinction. For <code>kind = task_board</code>,\n2025|<code>provider_manifest_id</code> MUST be null and\n2026|<code>task_board_bundle_id</code> MUST be non-null. Both-null and both-non-null\n2027|checkpoints are invalid.\n2028|\n2029|A checkpoint MUST NOT be published until every referenced object exists,\n2030|hashes correctly, passes schema validation, and the provider/task-board path\n2031|meets its quiescence requirement. A force takeover MAY select the newest\n2032|validated checkpoint even when no new safe checkpoint can be created.\n2033|\n2034|<code>event_heads</code> identifies the authoritative event DAG immediately\n2035|before the checkpoint object. A later <code>checkpoint.created</code> event MAY\n2036|reference that checkpoint and those heads; the checkpoint MUST NOT reference\n2037|the announcing event because that would create a circular digest dependency.\n2038|The transitive event-head closure also fixes the Section 2.4 effective\n2039|execution profile and its nullable source event for this checkpoint. A missing,\n2040|losing-lease, or non-newest <code>profile.changed</code> reference is\n2041|<code>integrity_failure</code>; checkpoint consumers MUST NOT consult a later\n2042|local-only profile event or fall back to the creation profile.\n2043|\n2044|Normative negative fixtures are: <code>CP-N1</code>, with\n2045|<code>background_idle = false</code> and status <code>validated</code>;\n2046|<code>CP-N2</code>, with a direct Session Record and null provider manifest;\n2047|<code>CP-N3</code>, with both persistence IDs non-null; and\n2048|<code>CP-N4</code>, with an unknown <code>safe_boundary.pid</code> member. Each\n2049|MUST be rejected with <code>incompatible_schema</code> before publication.\n2050|\n2051|Normative example:\n2052|\n2053|~~~json\n2054|{\n2055|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:checkpoint\",\n2056|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n2057|  \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n2058|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2059|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n2060|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n2061|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n2062|  \"safe_boundary\": {\n2063|    \"provider_id\": \"codex\",\n2064|    \"provider_version\": \"0.147.0\",\n2065|    \"evidence\": \"accepted_test\",\n2066|    \"input_blocked\": true,\n2067|    \"foreground_idle\": true,\n2068|    \"background_idle\": true,\n2069|    \"open_processes\": 0,\n2070|    \"open_database_handles\": 0\n2071|  },\n2072|  \"event_heads\": [\n2073|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n2074|  ],\n2075|  \"workspace_manifest_id\": \"sha256:a98ca90522b4de30e4aaaf9bf50529d09e15a817ffa67f94552fb313d1a1ad2e\",\n2076|  \"provider_manifest_id\": \"sha256:1e817955dcc529e282ab31f91c99561d03b3c5642282d2e0a0e05b0f60dd0f91\",\n2077|  \"task_board_bundle_id\": null,\n2078|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n2079|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:09:30.000Z\",\n2080|  \"status\": \"validated\",\n2081|  \"extensions\": {}\n2082|}\n2083|~~~\n2084|\n2085|### 5.5 Provider Identity Record\n2086|\n2087|The Provider Identity Record schema is\n2088|<code>urn:ax:schema:provider-identity</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Its\n2089|top-level object is closed and contains exactly:\n2090|\n2091|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n2092|| --- | --- | --- |\n2093|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Provider Identity schema identifier |\n2094|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n2095|| <code>record_id</code> | digest | Canonical object digest |\n2096|| <code>subject_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Equal to <code>session_id</code> |\n2097|| <code>session_id</code> | UUIDv7 | Existing logical session |\n2098|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id | Must equal the Session Record provider |\n2099|| <code>provider_version</code> | string[1..128] | Exact probed version |\n2100|| <code>provider_version_range</code> | string[1..256] | Adapter compatibility range used for this identity |\n2101|| <code>native_session_id</code> | string[1..512] | Opaque provider handle; never interpreted by core |\n2102|| <code>identity_kind</code> | enum | <code>session_uuid</code>, <code>session_path_or_id</code>, <code>backend_conversation_uuid</code>, <code>task_board_managed</code>, or <code>provider_defined</code> |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
