{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d267","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbc-2826-7673-94d4-717956fa0d32"},"sequence":1934,"recorded_at":1780531400003863,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"9162595d-8e13-449e-aede-0d31dd41754b"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Accepted CR-TASK-260830-14yo67-1 rev1. Task is now `integrating`; no commits made, no `commit_ack` supplied — `done` stays on the producer/integration side.\n\nWhat I verified with my own instruments (isolated copy, live tree untouched):\n\n- Spec fidelity: 16-member §5.4 shape matches `buildCandidate`; verbatim spec example re-attests to pinned digest `sha256:e05199…819656`; CP-N1..CP-N4 refuse `incompatible_schema` on both error layers. AC 8 of 8 driven.\n- Consumer admission: 8 reviewer probes through `Capture`/`Admit`/consumer — later-epoch head, wrong creator (`selector_observation_unavailable`), variant disagreement, moved bundle digest, wrong-type evidence member, unknown member, unknown session, re-identified later-head `Admit` — all refuse with exact codes. 6/6 probe tests pass.\n- Durability: hook tests + real-SIGKILL test pass twice each; blob-without-receipt resumes, receipt-without-blob errors (never admits), torn blob refuses; replay writes nothing; `-race` clean; `vet`, `tracecheck`, `cataloggen -check` clean; `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`/`sessquery` suites green.\n- Mutation: producer harness rerun 3× in isolation — 7/7 killed + control survived, exit 0. My own 5 narrowing mutants on untouched arms (foreign-lease, length-only blob compare, swallowed idle arm, swapped variant arms, counter bound) all killed. Four survivals all prove layered backstops (variant gate, head binding, owner shape, unreachable default) — reported in the verdict, not holes.\n- Refusal census: 44 of 47 arms directly driven; the 3 unreachable-by-construction arms have backstop proof.\n\nEvidence attached: `TASK-260830-14yo67_review-verdict-rev1.md` and `TASK-260830-14yo67_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz` (probe sources, logs, per-plant mutant logs).\n\nTwo non-blocking Story-close follow-ups recorded in the verdict: P2 — `section:5.4` registry gap text is stale and must be updated with a digest re-pin by a later leaf before `story_final` (producer correctly did not self-mint); P3 — README needs an `internal/sessckpt` section, and one forged-`Admit` foreign-lease negative would close the last mirror arm.","reason":null}}
